---
kind: scene
id: festival.night
title: The Lantern Festival
on: slotStart
priority: 30
when: "@festivalNight"
---

## The square

::bg{location="village_square" time="night"}
::music{action="start" mood="festive" volume="normal"}
@narrator: The whole mountain has come down to the square. The flat bell rings. Somebody's uncle is selling burnt almonds out of a wheelbarrow.

<match on="quest.forecast.state">
  <when is="complete">
    @narrator: Your forecast is still pinned to the notice board, four drawing pins, one per corner. Every string across the square is hung with lanterns.
    ::use{component="enter" who="elder" side="left"}
    @elder{emotion="happy"}: There she is — there's the forecast. Clear, you said. Look at it.
    ::vfx{type="lanterns"}
  </when>
  <when is="failed">
    @narrator: Only half the strings are hung. The committee hedged: lanterns on the east side, tarpaulins on the west, and a lot of people looking up.
    ::use{component="enter" who="elder" side="left"}
    @elder{emotion="stern"}: We waited for the station. The station was busy.
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    @narrator: Nobody quite knows whose job the forecast was. The lanterns go up anyway.
  </otherwise>
</match>

<match on="run.weather">
  <when is="storm">
    ::vfx{type="rain"}
    @narrator: And then it rains — a hard, sideways mountain rain — and the whole square runs for the hall laughing.
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    @narrator: The sky stays clear all night, hard and black and full of stars.
  </otherwise>
</match>

## The lanterns

<match on="quest.lantern.state">
  <when is="complete">
    ::clear
    ::use{component="enter" who="wren" side="right"}
    @wren{emotion="laughing"}: It's going! It's actually going!
    @narrator: Wren's lantern lifts off her palms — waxed paper, copper wire from a radio room, a storm candle from 1998 — and rises straight up, very steady, like it knows the way.
  </when>
  <when is="failed">
    @narrator: Wren stands at the edge of the square holding a shop lantern that says HAPPY BIRTHDAY on it. She lets it go anyway. It drifts sideways into a tree.
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    @narrator: A hundred lanterns go up from a hundred pairs of hands. None of them is yours.
  </otherwise>
</match>

## After

<match on="run.route">
  <when is="sol">
    ::clear
    ::use{component="enter" who="sol"}
    @sol{emotion="shy"}: I came down the mountain. I never come down the mountain. Don't tell the sky.
    @narrator: He counts the lanterns for you, out loud, and loses count at forty on purpose.
  </when>
  <when is="wren">
    ::clear
    ::use{component="enter" who="wren"}
    @wren{emotion="fond"}: Stay till the last one's gone? That's the rule. I just made it the rule.
  </when>
  <when is="none">
    ::clear
    ::use{component="enter" who="ines"}
    @ines{emotion="fond"}: Twenty-seven summers, then. Same time next year, intern?
  </when>
</match>

::set{user.summers += 1}
::set{run.summerOver = true}
::music{action="fadeOut"}
::end{reason="festivalOver"}
